Usage: agent-deck recall timeline <session> --json [--since <cursor> | --before <cursor> --limit N] [--limit N] [--tail N] [--agent <id>]
       agent-deck recall timeline --json --transcript <file> --harness claude|codex
       agent-deck recall timeline <session> --json --v1   (slice-6 turn shape)
<session>: deck session id, title or id prefix; a Claude/Codex conversation id; or #n / any id the index knows.
Rows are parsed from the native transcript directly, whatever the index or its deferral state. Needs [recall] enabled = true.
  -agent string
    	One Claude Code sub-agent sidechain by agent id
  -before string
    	Return older rows before this before_cursor (requires --limit N)
  -harness string
    	With --transcript: claude or codex
  -json
    	Output canonical JSON
  -limit int
    	Maximum older rows with --before; otherwise stop after N new rows and resume with --since
  -since string
    	Only what changed after this cursor: new rows in turns, changes to earlier rows in updates/removed
  -tail int
    	Only the last N rows, read from the end of the transcript (fast first paint)
  -transcript string
    	Read this Claude Code JSONL or Codex rollout instead of a session's
  -v1
    	Slice-6 output (turns with role/kind/text, turn frames) instead of rows
